From 76194b0c319566b54649cdef435173e5b07c6a99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rer integration <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:38:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Opt-in Rust package loading via pyrer.PackageRepository

New config `use_rer_package_loader` (default False; requires
use_rer_solver). When on, and the resolve has no package filter or user
package-load callback, and every packages_path entry is a filesystem
repository:

- RerSolver passes a per-process pyrer.PackageRepository to
  pyrer.solve; rez's loader remains the fallback per family
  (`load_family`) and per package (`load_package`).
- package_load_callback is still fired once per loaded package, so
  ResolvedContext.num_loaded_packages keeps counting.
- Resolved packages are built from the repository resource pyrer found
  them in, instead of re-listing the family through get_package().
- FileSystemPackageResource._load first tries pyrer.load_package_file
  (rez's own loader for anything pyrer hands back, or files written by
  this process); SourceCode values are rebuilt via __setstate__.
- package_repository_manager.clear_caches() also clears pyrer's caches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ZoN1vS65gdmG8gnnyUUem
